1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Scanning pools are useful if you have a need to limit which scanning machines can scan certain sites.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
You may wish to keep scanning machines and the sites they scan to the same geographic areas, for example.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Or some sites might only be available to scan by scanning machines on the same network.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Scanning pools stop the problem of a scan failing because the relevant machine is busy elsewhere,

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
or an assigned machine is unable to handle a restricted site for a scan.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Some example uses for scanning pools are

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Keeping the scanning machines and sites for one geographic area together,

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
coordinating off the resources for one team,

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
scanning sites with restricted access,

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,000
and reserving scanning machines for specific purposes, such as CI, CD pipelines or ad hoc scanning.

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Each scanning machine and site is assigned to a pool.

12
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The important features of scanning pools are

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Each scanning machine must belong to a scanning pool.

14
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Each site to be scanned must belong to a scanning pool.

15
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,000
And only scanning machines in the same pool as a site can scan that site.

16
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
To create a new scanning pool, do the following.

17
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
From the settings menu, select scanning machines,

18
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,000
click on the scanning pools tab,

19
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,000
select create pool,

20
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
provide a name and description for the new scanning pool,

21
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
assign the relevant scanning machines and sites to the new pool,

22
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,000
assign the relevant scanning machines and sites to the new pool,

23
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:31,000
and then click save.

24
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:39,000
To re-assign an existing scanning machine to a different pool, do the following.

25
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,000
From the settings menu, select scanning machines,

26
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
make sure you are on the scanning machines tab.

27
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
In the list of scanning machines,

28
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,000
select the relevant drop-down menu for the scanning machine you want to reassign,

29
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:02,000
and click on the name of the scanning pool to place it in that pool.

30
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:12,000
To re-assign an existing site to a different scanning pool, do the following.

31
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Click on the sites tab,

32
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
select the relevant site,

33
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,000
click on the details tab,

34
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
click edit,

35
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,000
click on the scanning pool drop-down,

36
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
and select the scanning pool you want the site to move to,

37
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
then click save.

38
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
click on the link to the scanning pool.

39
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Click save.

40
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Click save.

